{"title":"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Omega Learn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jerry cuts a wedge from a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-cm cylinder of bologna as shown by the dashed curve. Which answer choice is closest to the volume of his wedge in cubic centimeters?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db552e969b4c23a74bc8bb14087a79249bd36a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.65)); real d=90-63.43494882; draw(ellipse((origin), 2, 4)); fill((0,4)--(0,-4)--(-8,-4)--(-8,4)--cycle, white); draw(ellipse((-4,0), 2, 4)); draw((0,4)--(-4,4)); draw((0,-4)--(-4,-4)); draw(shift(-2,0)*rotate(-d-5)*ellipse(origin, 1.82, 4.56), linetype(&quot;10 10&quot;)); draw((-4,4)--(-8,4), dashed); draw((-4,-4)--(-8,-4), dashed); draw((-4,4.3)--(-4,5)); draw((0,4.3)--(0,5)); draw((-7,4)--(-7,-4), Arrows(5)); draw((-4,4.7)--(0,4.7), Arrows(5)); label(&quot;$8$ cm&quot;, (-7,0), W); label(&quot;$6$ cm&quot;, (-2,4.7), N);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea47f06f15f579defbe1060951bf2179b4c290ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\ 48 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)} \\ 75 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)} \\ 151\\qquad \\textbf{(D)} \\ 192 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)} \\ 603$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The slice is cutting the cylinder into two equal wedges with equal volume. The cylinder's volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f1944b0416d3d116357c7081fd618bc37b54a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2 h = \\pi (4^2)(6) = 96\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"19\" />. The volume of the wedge is half this which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/312221d550873f662787d5d3c8e259cd9a5e6d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48\\pi \\approx \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 151}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"126\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The volume of the whole cylinder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffd03904b2515ee60aef50b9e1c38b88394af311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. We approximate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, meaning our answer will be slightly too small. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3bef57dfd00556d43ab69e4e63f97b084d31cd2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96*3=288$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"14\" />, and we know the wedge cuts the cylinder perfectly in half. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a4d74be279cdf3b543a99c8b610d6d4036fd93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$288/2 = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />, so the closest answer choice that is greater than that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717893dfe1b2ebfb35b29f974f141669eb4fb317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 151}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Lightning_Fox, Imdrowninginmath\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn\">Video Solution by Omega Learn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Omega Learn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FDgcLW4frg8?t=2556\">https://youtu.be/FDgcLW4frg8?t=2556</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q7OCpOn1abY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q7OCpOn1abY</a>   ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 8\">2008 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=20